{
  "$comment": "Pure function vectors: input in, output out, no client or transport. Every SDK's runner calls its own version of each function and compares. Outputs are JSON: a missing key and null both mean 'absent'. Errors are {\"error\": \"<kind>\"}; each language maps the kind to its own error type. Format: see vectors.md.",
  "rateLimit": {
    "$comment": "parseRateLimit(headers, now). Header names are already lowercased. Reads RateLimit and RateLimit-Policy (structured lists; a quoted name may contain , ; and =). The entry named 'daily' fills `daily`; any other entry is the tier and fills `burst`, with perMinute = q / (w / 60) and w defaulting to 60. Values must be non-negative integers that fit in 2^53 - 1; anything else is ignored without dropping the other params. When both IETF headers are empty or absent, fall back to the X-RateLimit-* headers, whose resets are epoch seconds turned into seconds from `now` (never below 0). No rate-limit headers at all gives null.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "ietf headers",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "\"Free\";q=60;w=60;burst=10, \"daily\";q=5000;w=86400",
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=9;t=1, \"daily\";r=4999;t=86000"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10,
            "perMinute": 60,
            "remaining": 9,
            "resetSeconds": 1
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 5000,
            "remaining": 4999,
            "resetSeconds": 86000
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "tier entry dropped once the daily cap is spent",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "\"Supporter\";q=60;w=60;burst=15, \"daily\";q=50000;w=86400",
            "ratelimit": "\"daily\";r=0;t=40000"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Supporter",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 15,
            "perMinute": 60
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 50000,
            "remaining": 0,
            "resetSeconds": 40000
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "quoted tier name with a suffix",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "\"Free (JWT)\";q=60;w=60;burst=5, \"daily\";q=5000;w=86400",
            "ratelimit": "\"Free (JWT)\";r=4;t=1, \"daily\";r=10;t=100"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free (JWT)",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 5,
            "perMinute": 60,
            "remaining": 4,
            "resetSeconds": 1
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 5000,
            "remaining": 10,
            "resetSeconds": 100
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "quoted tier name containing , ; and =",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "\"Supporter, Annual; seats=2\";q=60;w=60;burst=5, \"daily\";q=5000;w=86400",
            "ratelimit": "\"Supporter, Annual; seats=2\";r=4;t=1, \"daily\";r=10;t=100"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Supporter, Annual; seats=2",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 5,
            "perMinute": 60,
            "remaining": 4,
            "resetSeconds": 1
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 5000,
            "remaining": 10,
            "resetSeconds": 100
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "perMinute scales by the window",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "\"Free\";q=60;w=30;burst=10"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10,
            "perMinute": 120
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "empty value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "exponent value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=1e3;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "negative value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=-1;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "decimal value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=1.5;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "hex value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=0x10;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "word value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=abc;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "value past 2^53 - 1 ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=9007199254740992;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "huge value ignored",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=99999999999999999999999999999999;t=1"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 1
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "params after a malformed one are kept",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=oops;bogus;t=3, \"daily\";r=1;t=2"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "resetSeconds": 3
          },
          "daily": {
            "remaining": 1,
            "resetSeconds": 2
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "extra whitespace around items and params",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": " \"Free\" ; q = 60 ; burst = 10 ,  \"daily\";q=5000 ",
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=9;t=1,\"daily\";r=4999;t=86000"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10,
            "perMinute": 60,
            "remaining": 9,
            "resetSeconds": 1
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 5000,
            "remaining": 4999,
            "resetSeconds": 86000
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "entries merge by name in any order",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "\"daily\";q=5000;w=86400, \"Free\";q=60;w=60;burst=10",
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=9;t=1, \"daily\";r=4999;t=86000"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10,
            "perMinute": 60,
            "remaining": 9,
            "resetSeconds": 1
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 5000,
            "remaining": 4999,
            "resetSeconds": 86000
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "RateLimit without RateLimit-Policy",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit": "\"Free\";r=9;t=1, \"daily\";r=4999;t=86000"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "tier": "Free",
          "burst": {
            "remaining": 9,
            "resetSeconds": 1
          },
          "daily": {
            "remaining": 4999,
            "resetSeconds": 86000
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "legacy X-RateLimit headers",
        "in": {
          "now": 1800000000,
          "headers": {
            "x-ratelimit-limit": "10",
            "x-ratelimit-remaining": "7",
            "x-ratelimit-reset": "1800000003",
            "x-ratelimit-daily-limit": "5000",
            "x-ratelimit-daily-remaining": "4990",
            "x-ratelimit-daily-reset": "1800000500"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10,
            "remaining": 7,
            "resetSeconds": 3
          },
          "daily": {
            "limit": 5000,
            "remaining": 4990,
            "resetSeconds": 500
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "legacy reset in the past clamps to 0",
        "in": {
          "now": 1800000000,
          "headers": {
            "x-ratelimit-limit": "10",
            "x-ratelimit-reset": "1799999990"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10,
            "resetSeconds": 0
          },
          "daily": {}
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "legacy used when the IETF headers are blank",
        "in": {
          "now": 0,
          "headers": {
            "ratelimit-policy": "",
            "ratelimit": " ",
            "x-ratelimit-limit": "10"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10
          },
          "daily": {}
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "non-integer legacy values ignored",
        "in": {
          "now": 0,
          "headers": {
            "x-ratelimit-limit": "10",
            "x-ratelimit-remaining": "",
            "x-ratelimit-daily-limit": "1e3"
          }
        },
        "out": {
          "burst": {
            "limit": 10
          },
          "daily": {}
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "no rate-limit headers",
        "in": {
          "headers": {
            "content-type": "application/json"
          }
        },
        "out": null
      }
    ]
  },
  "requestCost": {
    "$comment": "requestCost(query): what the gateway charges. One per top-level field of the operation (the first query, mutation, subscription or bare { }; fragment definitions are skipped). Aliases count by their field. A top-level fragment spread counts one. __schema, __type, __typename and insert_reading_journal are free unless reached through a spread. Text inside strings, block strings and comments is ignored. The result is never below 1. No GraphQL parser is needed; a scanner is enough.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "one root, however deep",
        "in": "query GetLibrary($userId: Int!) { user_books(where: { user_id: { _eq: $userId } }) { id book { id editions(limit: 1) { id } } user_book_reads { id } } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "fragment definitions before the operation are skipped",
        "in": "fragment B on books { id title } fragment E on editions { id } query GetBook($id: Int!) { books_by_pk(id: $id) { ...B editions { ...E } } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "a top-level spread counts one",
        "in": "fragment R on query_root { books { id } } query Q { ...R lists { id } }",
        "out": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "aliased roots in a batch",
        "in": "mutation M($b0: ListBookInput!, $b1: ListBookInput!) { b0: insert_list_book(object: $b0) { id } b1: insert_list_book(object: $b1) { id } }",
        "out": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "unaliased roots with arguments and nested selections",
        "in": "query D($u: Int!) {\n  books(limit: 1, where: { slug: { _is_null: false } }) { id editions(limit: 1) { id } }\n  lists(limit: 1, where: { user_id: { _eq: $u } }) { id }\n  user_books(limit: 1) { id }\n}",
        "out": 3
      },
      {
        "name": "directives are not fields",
        "in": "query Q($a: Boolean!) { books @include(if: $a) { id } lists @skip(if: $a) { id } }",
        "out": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "braces and words inside strings and comments",
        "in": "query { # a { b } c\n search(query: \"x { y } z\", per_page: 1) { ids } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "block string",
        "in": "query { search(query: \"\"\"a { b } c\"\"\") { ids } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "introspection is free but the minimum is 1",
        "in": "query { __schema { types { name } } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "insert_reading_journal is free but the minimum is 1",
        "in": "mutation { insert_reading_journal(object: {}) { id } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "aliased free fields stay free",
        "in": "mutation { a: insert_reading_journal(object: {}) { id } b: insert_reading_journal(object: {}) { id } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "free field next to a paid one",
        "in": "mutation { insert_reading_journal(object: {}) { id } other: delete_list(id: 1) { success } }",
        "out": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "two paid aliases",
        "in": "mutation { x: delete_list(id: 1) { success } y: delete_list(id: 2) { success } }",
        "out": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "empty text",
        "in": "",
        "out": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "token": {
    "$comment": "normalizeToken(raw): clean a pasted static token, then check it against shared/auth.json tokens.prefixes in order. Cleanup: trim whitespace, drop a leading 'Bearer' (any case) followed by whitespace or the end, trim again. `in` null means no token was given. Outputs: {\"token\"} on success; plus \"warning\": <prefix> when a warn rule matched (send that rule's message to the warning callback); {\"error\": \"missingToken\"} with auth.json missingMessage; {\"error\": \"refusedToken\", \"prefix\": <prefix>} with that rule's message. Unknown formats pass through: the server decides.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "whitespace and newlines trimmed",
        "in": "  hc_pat_abc123\n",
        "out": {
          "token": "hc_pat_abc123"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "tabs and CRLF trimmed",
        "in": "\thc_pat_abc123\r\n",
        "out": {
          "token": "hc_pat_abc123"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "Bearer prefix dropped",
        "in": "Bearer hc_pat_abc123",
        "out": {
          "token": "hc_pat_abc123"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "bearer prefix in any case, extra spaces",
        "in": "bearer   hc_pat_abc123",
        "out": {
          "token": "hc_pat_abc123"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "BEARER prefix",
        "in": "BEARER hc_at_xyz",
        "out": {
          "token": "hc_at_xyz"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "Bearer glued to the token is not a prefix",
        "in": "Bearerhc_pat_abc",
        "out": {
          "token": "Bearerhc_pat_abc"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "unknown format passes through",
        "in": "hc_newtype_xyz",
        "out": {
          "token": "hc_newtype_xyz"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "legacy JWT warns",
        "in": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.e30.x",
        "out": {
          "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.e30.x",
          "warning": "eyJ"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "legacy JWT after Bearer warns",
        "in": " Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.e30.x ",
        "out": {
          "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.e30.x",
          "warning": "eyJ"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "missing",
        "in": null,
        "out": {
          "error": "missingToken"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "empty",
        "in": "",
        "out": {
          "error": "missingToken"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "whitespace only",
        "in": "  \n",
        "out": {
          "error": "missingToken"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "only a Bearer prefix",
        "in": "Bearer ",
        "out": {
          "error": "missingToken"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "bare Bearer",
        "in": "Bearer",
        "out": {
          "error": "missingToken"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "refresh token refused",
        "in": "hc_rt_abc",
        "out": {
          "error": "refusedToken",
          "prefix": "hc_rt_"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "refresh token after Bearer refused",
        "in": "Bearer hc_rt_abc",
        "out": {
          "error": "refusedToken",
          "prefix": "hc_rt_"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "authorization code refused",
        "in": "hc_ac_abc",
        "out": {
          "error": "refusedToken",
          "prefix": "hc_ac_"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "isbn": {
    "$comment": "cleanIsbn(code): drop whitespace and hyphens, uppercase (an ISBN-10 may end in x). It does not validate length or check digits; exact lookups need neither. Inputs here are ASCII.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "hyphenated ISBN-13",
        "in": "978-0-593-13520-4",
        "out": "9780593135204"
      },
      {
        "name": "spaces and lowercase x",
        "in": "0 8044 2957 x",
        "out": "080442957X"
      },
      {
        "name": "surrounding whitespace and newline",
        "in": "  9780593135204\n",
        "out": "9780593135204"
      },
      {
        "name": "tab",
        "in": "0593\t135202",
        "out": "0593135202"
      },
      {
        "name": "already clean",
        "in": "9780345539786",
        "out": "9780345539786"
      },
      {
        "name": "no validation",
        "in": "978-0-000-00000-0",
        "out": "9780000000000"
      }
    ]
  },
  "localDate": {
    "$comment": "localDate(instant, timeZone): the calendar date YYYY-MM-DD at `instant` (ISO 8601 UTC) in IANA `timeZone`, zero-padded. The API stores user dates as local dates, not UTC. Must not depend on the runtime's locale or default timezone.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "behind UTC rolls back a day",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-09-29T02:30:00Z",
          "timeZone": "America/Denver"
        },
        "out": "2026-09-28"
      },
      {
        "name": "ahead of UTC",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-09-29T02:30:00Z",
          "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
        },
        "out": "2026-09-29"
      },
      {
        "name": "UTC",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-09-29T02:30:00Z",
          "timeZone": "UTC"
        },
        "out": "2026-09-29"
      },
      {
        "name": "zero-padded month and day",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-01-05T12:00:00Z",
          "timeZone": "UTC"
        },
        "out": "2026-01-05"
      },
      {
        "name": "half-hour offset, before midnight",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-09-28T18:29:00Z",
          "timeZone": "Asia/Kolkata"
        },
        "out": "2026-09-28"
      },
      {
        "name": "half-hour offset, after midnight",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-09-28T18:30:00Z",
          "timeZone": "Asia/Kolkata"
        },
        "out": "2026-09-29"
      },
      {
        "name": "+14 crosses the year",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-12-31T10:30:00Z",
          "timeZone": "Pacific/Kiritimati"
        },
        "out": "2027-01-01"
      },
      {
        "name": "daylight saving day",
        "in": {
          "instant": "2026-03-08T07:30:00Z",
          "timeZone": "America/New_York"
        },
        "out": "2026-03-08"
      }
    ]
  },
  "goalProgress": {
    "$comment": "goalProgress({metric, goal, progress}): progress and target in the goal's own unit. Hour goals store the target in hours but the API reports progress in seconds, so current = progress / 3600 for metric 'hour'. percent = current / target * 100, or 0 when the target is 0 or less. Not clamped: over 100 is allowed. Compare numbers within 1e-9.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "books",
        "in": {
          "metric": "book",
          "goal": 50,
          "progress": 10
        },
        "out": {
          "current": 10,
          "target": 50,
          "percent": 20
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "pages",
        "in": {
          "metric": "page",
          "goal": 5000,
          "progress": 1250
        },
        "out": {
          "current": 1250,
          "target": 5000,
          "percent": 25
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "hours from seconds, past 100%",
        "in": {
          "metric": "hour",
          "goal": 14,
          "progress": 73837
        },
        "out": {
          "current": 20.510277777777777,
          "target": 14,
          "percent": 146.50198412698413
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "zero target",
        "in": {
          "metric": "book",
          "goal": 0,
          "progress": 3
        },
        "out": {
          "current": 3,
          "target": 0,
          "percent": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "zero target in hours",
        "in": {
          "metric": "hour",
          "goal": 0,
          "progress": 3600
        },
        "out": {
          "current": 1,
          "target": 0,
          "percent": 0
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "libraryCursor": {
    "$comment": "The library.changes cursor: '<updated_at>|<id>' of the last row seen. Keep updated_at as the server's string (it has microseconds, which most date types round). Decode splits at the LAST '|'; the part before must be non-empty and the part after an integer, otherwise {\"error\": \"invalidCursor\"} (the language's argument error). Treat the cursor as opaque everywhere else.",
    "encode": [
      {
        "name": "keeps microseconds",
        "in": {
          "updatedAt": "2026-10-07T02:00:00.654321+00:00",
          "id": 2
        },
        "out": "2026-10-07T02:00:00.654321+00:00|2"
      }
    ],
    "decode": [
      {
        "name": "round trip",
        "in": "2026-10-07T01:00:00.123456+00:00|7",
        "out": {
          "after": "2026-10-07T01:00:00.123456+00:00",
          "afterId": 7
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "splits at the last bar",
        "in": "a|b|3",
        "out": {
          "after": "a|b",
          "afterId": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "no bar",
        "in": "2026-10-07",
        "out": {
          "error": "invalidCursor"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "empty timestamp",
        "in": "|5",
        "out": {
          "error": "invalidCursor"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "id not a number",
        "in": "2026-10-07|abc",
        "out": {
          "error": "invalidCursor"
        }
